WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:04.710
CHU2 sent us a list of dates to choose from
for the big showdown.

00:00:04.710 --> 00:00:05.830
When?

00:00:05.830 --> 00:00:08.580
Looks like next Friday, Saturday, and Sunday.

00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:11.580
Hold on... Isn't that before the
"Over the Future" concert?

00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:13.330
Our performance at "Over the Future"

00:00:13.330 --> 00:00:17.420
is a key factor in determining our
preparedness for FUTURE WORLD FES.

00:00:17.790 --> 00:00:20.460
We ought to concentrate on
the more important matter at hand.

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:23.000
Should I send her a list of different dates, Yukina?

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:26.880
No. Schedule us for next Friday.

00:00:28.330 --> 00:00:29.420
Are you sure?!

00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:32.250
She knows exactly what she's doing.

00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:36.000
Alright, you can count on me!

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:37.710
Let's kick some butt, Rin-Rin!

00:00:37.710 --> 00:00:38.880
R-right.

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:42.500
At least we'll be able to focus on the concert
once we've gotten this performance out of the way...

00:00:43.130 --> 00:00:46.080
Better cancel our plans for Friday...

00:00:46.540 --> 00:00:49.250
I'll be sure to let Marina-san know.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:57.880
Initial honki no jibun yuzurenakute

00:00:57.880 --> 00:01:02.710
Shoudou yubisaki kara emotion!

00:01:12.580 --> 00:01:17.330
Ano hi watashi wa shoujo demo otona demo naku

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:22.290
Majirike no nai manazashi de yume dake miteta

00:01:22.630 --> 00:01:27.330
Meramera yurayurari moetagiru yoru

00:01:27.540 --> 00:01:32.380
Yuuki o kamishimete tabi ni detanda

00:01:32.710 --> 00:01:37.710
Initial hajimete wakiagatta mono wa

00:01:37.710 --> 00:01:42.500
Furue karadajuu kara emotion

00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:47.420
Naze ni hatenaki yozora ni mukatte

00:01:47.420 --> 00:01:53.290
Nandomo onnaji kotoba o sakebitsuzukeru no ka?

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:57.170
Toki ni aimai de miushinau

00:01:57.170 --> 00:02:00.000
Tomadoigachi na jibun demo

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:04.420
"Te ni shita mono" wa imademo koko ni

00:02:04.630 --> 00:02:07.080
Initial no sono saki e

00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:09.500
Hoshi no kodou kanjite

00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:14.170
(Kimi wa) tsuyoku kakinarashiteiru

00:02:14.170 --> 00:02:17.170
(Ima mo) kokoro furuwasete

00:02:17.170 --> 00:02:19.040
Aishiteiru!

00:02:20.790 --> 00:02:22.460
The two of you are performing at
the same show?

00:02:22.710 --> 00:02:26.040
Yup! You came to our self-sponsored concert, right?

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:27.040
It's the same venue!

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:28.210
Gotcha...

00:02:28.670 --> 00:02:30.630
Meanwhile, this one's STILL practicing.

00:02:31.830 --> 00:02:34.920
I've got rehearsal at CHU2-san's studio today...

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:37.790
I've been practicing nonstop at home, lately!

00:02:38.790 --> 00:02:40.210
CHU2, eh?

00:02:40.210 --> 00:02:41.710
Are you feeling alright?

00:02:42.540 --> 00:02:44.790
The girl practically hunted you down.

00:02:44.790 --> 00:02:46.630
Is she putting too much pressure on you?

00:02:48.880 --> 00:02:51.290
This is my first live performance as a member of RAS.

00:02:51.290 --> 00:02:53.040
Gotta give it the ol' college try!

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:54.670
Me, too!

00:02:54.920 --> 00:02:57.000
Bask in my glory...

00:02:57.000 --> 00:02:58.330
And, uh...

00:02:58.330 --> 00:03:01.630
Feast thine eyes on the coolest performance
thou shalt ever see!

00:03:01.630 --> 00:03:03.500
Yes, my liege!

00:03:03.500 --> 00:03:04.880
So, um...

00:03:04.880 --> 00:03:07.040
Would you mind if I came, too?

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:08.000
Huh?!

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:10.000
You're going to come watch us, Asuka-chan?!

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:12.040
As long as it doesn't interfere
with my study schedule...

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:13.080
Hooray!

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:13.920
Ako...!

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:15.210
I'll save you a seat!

00:03:15.210 --> 00:03:16.710
Me, too!

00:03:16.710 --> 00:03:17.790
Jeez...

00:03:18.540 --> 00:03:21.540
Rinko:

00:03:18.540 --> 00:03:21.540
Made a few adjustments to my keyboard.

00:03:18.540 --> 00:03:21.540
Mind checking it out at our next session?

00:03:18.540 --> 00:03:21.540
Lisa:

00:03:18.540 --> 00:03:21.540
Roger!

00:03:18.550 --> 00:03:21.540
Got a message from CHU2. She wants to meet up

00:03:18.550 --> 00:03:21.540
with us at CiRCLE after school. Should we go?

00:03:18.550 --> 00:03:21.540
Rinko:

00:03:18.550 --> 00:03:21.540
Sure thing.

00:03:18.550 --> 00:03:21.540
Supreme Mage of Darkness Ako:

00:03:25.420 --> 00:03:26.540
Excuse us!

00:03:27.330 --> 00:03:29.460
Rinko-senpai, Sayo-senpai!

00:03:30.380 --> 00:03:31.790
What's with all the shouting?

00:03:31.790 --> 00:03:33.290
Is this video for real?!

00:03:35.460 --> 00:03:36.420
Oops...

00:03:36.420 --> 00:03:37.710
Oh, CHU2-sama!

00:03:38.580 --> 00:03:40.250
Hello, everyone.

00:03:40.250 --> 00:03:43.540
My name is CHU2.
I'm the producer of RAISE A SUILEN.

00:03:43.830 --> 00:03:47.000
Have you been enjoying
the "BanG Dream" tournament?

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:48.040
Now then...

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:53.330
Our upcoming performance on November 15th
is set to take place at Dub.

00:03:53.330 --> 00:03:57.500
We've selected the current frontrunner,
Roselia, as our opponent.

00:03:57.880 --> 00:04:00.750
This one-on-one battle isn't just about the tournament.

00:04:00.750 --> 00:04:03.290
We're going to shake the Girl Band Generation.

00:04:03.290 --> 00:04:06.540
Calling this a defining moment
would be an understatement.

00:04:06.830 --> 00:04:09.670
A few days ago, you saw our MV.

00:04:09.670 --> 00:04:13.420
As you know, we've recruited ourselves
a sweet new guitarist.

00:04:13.630 --> 00:04:15.630
We invite you to witness RAISE A SUILEN

00:04:15.630 --> 00:04:20.210
as we evolve and blast our way
to the top of the music scene.

00:04:21.920 --> 00:04:24.000
Prepare yourselves, Roselia.

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:25.130
This is it.

00:04:30.290 --> 00:04:32.290
You put me in a tough spot...

00:04:32.290 --> 00:04:35.170
Not to mention the trouble
this might cause for the other bands...

00:04:35.170 --> 00:04:36.750
No problem!

00:04:36.750 --> 00:04:39.630
There won't be entries from any other bands.

00:04:39.630 --> 00:04:40.380
Huh?

00:04:41.710 --> 00:04:43.580
They've seen the caliber of our performances thus far.

00:04:43.580 --> 00:04:46.580
They know exactly what we're capable of.

00:04:47.080 --> 00:04:50.830
After our declaration of war against Roselia,

00:04:50.830 --> 00:04:54.330
what band in their right mind
would dare to challenge us?

00:04:54.330 --> 00:04:55.880
"Declar..."?

00:04:57.500 --> 00:04:59.710
The entry deadline is...

00:04:59.710 --> 00:05:00.630
PAREO.

00:05:00.630 --> 00:05:02.000
Right away, CHU2-sama!

00:05:02.960 --> 00:05:07.130
Accepting entries until 6:00PM

00:05:02.960 --> 00:05:07.130
Entries received: 2

00:05:03.290 --> 00:05:06.380
3, 2, 1.

00:05:06.380 --> 00:05:07.710
Time's up.

00:05:07.130 --> 00:05:08.250
Accepting entries until 6:00PM

00:05:07.130 --> 00:05:08.250
CLOSED FOR ENTRIES

00:05:07.130 --> 00:05:08.250
Entries received: 2

00:05:08.710 --> 00:05:12.250
This is officially a duel between RAS and Roselia.

00:05:14.290 --> 00:05:17.420
So, you posted that video
knowing what would happen?

00:05:17.420 --> 00:05:18.420
Yes!

00:05:18.420 --> 00:05:23.290
Give our fans something to buzz about
and boost public interest in the tournament itself.

00:05:23.290 --> 00:05:26.000
A win-win from a promotional standpoint,
don't you think?

00:05:27.380 --> 00:05:30.040
I suppose you aren't breaking the rules...

00:05:30.330 --> 00:05:33.000
Just make sure you don't do anything risky, okay?

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:35.630
Of course! Thanks, Marina.

00:05:35.630 --> 00:05:37.670
Allow me to review our agreement:

00:05:37.670 --> 00:05:39.170
We're performing at Dub.

00:05:39.170 --> 00:05:42.920
Using the voting system in place
for the tournament's preliminary round,

00:05:42.920 --> 00:05:46.170
the winner will be determined
based on number of votes received.

00:05:46.170 --> 00:05:49.670
In other words,
the audience chooses their favorite band.

00:05:49.670 --> 00:05:51.080
Who's performing first?

00:05:51.080 --> 00:05:54.960
The final act of a show tends to leave
a lasting impression...

00:05:54.960 --> 00:05:56.710
Do you have a preference?

00:05:57.080 --> 00:05:58.920
Doesn't matter to us.

00:06:00.130 --> 00:06:02.630
In that case, I'd like to make a suggestion...

00:06:05.920 --> 00:06:10.960
Each band receives a score based on a
popularity survey posted at the entrance of the venue.

00:06:10.960 --> 00:06:13.290
Whoever gets a higher score goes second.

00:06:13.290 --> 00:06:16.830
The crowd favorite earns the right
to be the final act, basically...

00:06:16.830 --> 00:06:19.750
Which means we won't know
until the day of the performance, right?

00:06:19.750 --> 00:06:21.250
Don't worry, Rin-Rin!

00:06:21.250 --> 00:06:24.960
Either way, we just have to put on
an awesome show!

00:06:24.960 --> 00:06:27.040
Yes. That's exactly right, Ako.

00:06:27.420 --> 00:06:29.630
We're going to prepare two setlists.

00:06:30.290 --> 00:06:31.500
First or last...

00:06:31.500 --> 00:06:34.250
The order is irrelevant.
Our performance will be flawless.

00:06:34.250 --> 00:06:35.210
Right!

00:06:35.210 --> 00:06:37.210
Yikes, talk about rough...

00:06:37.210 --> 00:06:38.080
Huh?

00:06:38.080 --> 00:06:40.880
Different setlists require different stage settings.

00:06:40.880 --> 00:06:43.790
And having two sets of songs
means double the practice.

00:06:43.790 --> 00:06:44.710
Double?!

00:06:44.710 --> 00:06:46.670
Y..Yukina-san...!

00:06:46.670 --> 00:06:50.580
We have to be careful not to get confused
with our "Over the Future" setlist...

00:06:50.580 --> 00:06:53.080
Think we should be doing some sort of publicity?

00:06:53.080 --> 00:06:54.830
I'll invite all of my friends!

00:06:54.830 --> 00:06:57.080
More importantly, we need to
keep up with our practice.

00:06:57.080 --> 00:06:59.500
And which practice would that be?

00:07:00.710 --> 00:07:02.580
For "Over the Future"?

00:07:02.580 --> 00:07:04.960
Or the "BanG Dream" preliminaries?

00:07:07.580 --> 00:07:10.420
I don't understand why you're even
entertaining this nonsense.

00:07:10.420 --> 00:07:12.580
You're neglecting FUTURE WORLD FES.

00:07:13.790 --> 00:07:17.880
You said that girl reminds you of
your younger self, right?

00:07:17.880 --> 00:07:18.920
That's right.

00:07:18.920 --> 00:07:19.710
Sayo...

00:07:19.710 --> 00:07:22.130
Is that why you've decided to humor her?

00:07:22.420 --> 00:07:25.420
Is this competition truly in Roselia's best interest?

00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:28.630
C'mon, you two...

00:07:28.630 --> 00:07:30.250
Let's start practicing.

00:07:30.250 --> 00:07:31.170
Okay?

00:07:31.170 --> 00:07:32.170
No.

00:07:32.170 --> 00:07:35.540
I don't believe our current situation
will result in a productive session.

00:07:35.540 --> 00:07:36.710
Agreed.

00:07:37.040 --> 00:07:38.630
R..Rin-Rin...

00:07:38.630 --> 00:07:39.830
U-um...

00:07:39.830 --> 00:07:41.500
This is a waste of time.

00:07:41.500 --> 00:07:43.500
I'll practice at home for today.

00:07:43.500 --> 00:07:44.290
Sayo!

00:07:47.040 --> 00:07:48.750
Wait up, Sayo!

00:07:48.750 --> 00:07:51.380
Do you approve of this, Imai-san?

00:07:52.420 --> 00:07:55.630
Well... to be honest, I can't say I totally understand.

00:07:55.630 --> 00:07:58.500
But Yukina seems determined
to see this thing through...

00:07:58.500 --> 00:08:01.670
I figured she's having a hard time
letting it slide or something.

00:08:02.170 --> 00:08:04.670
Minato-san is far too lenient.

00:08:08.330 --> 00:08:10.130
Huh? Sayo-san...?

00:08:10.130 --> 00:08:11.330
Oh my...

00:08:23.750 --> 00:08:25.330
Hey, Big Sis!

00:08:25.330 --> 00:08:27.500
Are you seriously gonna compete against RAS?

00:08:27.500 --> 00:08:29.580
Can't you knock quietly, Hina?

00:08:29.580 --> 00:08:31.830
I wanna go! Can I?

00:08:32.210 --> 00:08:33.630
If your schedule permits...

00:08:33.630 --> 00:08:35.580
For real?! Yippee!

00:08:35.580 --> 00:08:37.330
The news kinda surprised me, though.

00:08:37.330 --> 00:08:41.290
I thought you were too busy
getting ready for "Over the Future."

00:08:42.710 --> 00:08:44.710
I thought so, too...

00:08:48.250 --> 00:08:52.080
I get it... So that's what Yukina-chan's up to.

00:08:52.330 --> 00:08:54.880
That girl is taking advantage of her kindness.

00:08:54.880 --> 00:08:57.290
I knew I should've been the one
to handle negotiations...

00:08:58.500 --> 00:08:59.750
Should we pay her a visit?

00:09:00.460 --> 00:09:01.330
What?

00:09:02.040 --> 00:09:03.750
Ramen GINGA

00:09:04.290 --> 00:09:05.630
Welcome!

00:09:10.750 --> 00:09:12.960
Hey. Fancy meeting you here.

00:09:13.710 --> 00:09:15.380
"Princess Fried Rice."

00:09:15.670 --> 00:09:17.170
Thanks a lot.

00:09:19.540 --> 00:09:20.540
Not bad.

00:09:20.540 --> 00:09:21.460
Right?

00:09:21.460 --> 00:09:24.130
You need anything else?
How 'bout an egg on top?

00:09:25.880 --> 00:09:27.080
I'm fine.

00:09:27.670 --> 00:09:29.960
Don't see you in the shop very often.

00:09:30.210 --> 00:09:32.750
Yeah... I was hoping we could talk.

00:09:36.330 --> 00:09:38.380
We made it!

00:09:38.380 --> 00:09:39.380
Seriously?

00:09:39.380 --> 00:09:40.630
Yup, this is the place!

00:09:40.630 --> 00:09:41.790
That's not what I meant.

00:09:41.790 --> 00:09:44.420
Are you sure we should just barge in
without an appointment?

00:09:44.420 --> 00:09:47.250
We ring the doorbell,
and if she doesn't come out, we go home!

00:09:47.250 --> 00:09:48.330
What...?

00:09:49.250 --> 00:09:52.290
"Ready, go... Let it go..."

00:09:52.290 --> 00:09:55.630
CHU2-sama! Why not take a break?

00:09:55.630 --> 00:09:58.130
CHU2-sama!

00:09:58.960 --> 00:10:01.330
Is this a camera? It totally is!

00:10:01.330 --> 00:10:03.580
Yoo-hoo! Are you home, CHU2-chan?

00:10:03.580 --> 00:10:04.920
Hey!

00:10:05.080 --> 00:10:06.670
H..Hina-chan?!

00:10:06.670 --> 00:10:07.750
Hina Hikawa?!

00:10:07.750 --> 00:10:09.630
Hina-chan! I can't believe it!

00:10:10.580 --> 00:10:13.380
Oh, my goodness! I've got to go change
the color of my hair!

00:10:13.380 --> 00:10:15.330
No! Answer the door!

00:10:15.330 --> 00:10:17.000
B-but I...!

00:10:20.420 --> 00:10:21.790
Welcome!

00:10:23.040 --> 00:10:24.460
Reona-chan!

00:10:25.500 --> 00:10:28.040
I'm honored that you remember me!

00:10:28.040 --> 00:10:30.790
However, it's pronounced "PAREO."

00:10:30.790 --> 00:10:34.670
Unfortunately, my hair doesn't match yours.
Please forgive my rudeness...

00:10:34.670 --> 00:10:35.790
No worries!

00:10:37.210 --> 00:10:40.380
Welcome, Hina Hikawa and Sayo Hikawa!

00:10:40.380 --> 00:10:43.830
Your house sure is fancy, CHU2-san!

00:10:43.830 --> 00:10:47.580
Shall we take a tour of the studio?
I'd love to see your guitar skills in action-

00:10:47.580 --> 00:10:51.040
My apologies, but we haven't
come here to fool around.

00:10:51.170 --> 00:10:54.670
Oh, that's right! My big sis has something
she wants to talk to you about.

00:10:55.040 --> 00:10:59.040
Declaring a winner at our upcoming performance
has no bearing on the quality of our music.

00:10:59.040 --> 00:11:02.880
One band is not objectively superior
or inferior to the other.

00:11:03.080 --> 00:11:06.040
Therefore, the entire thing is meaningless.

00:11:06.040 --> 00:11:07.830
You're incorrect, I'm afraid.

00:11:08.330 --> 00:11:13.420
Beating you in a competition would serve as
evidence that my band is better than Roselia,

00:11:13.420 --> 00:11:15.460
and this is my chance to do it.

00:11:15.460 --> 00:11:19.790
If we compare the number of votes from the audience,
no one would be able to deny the results.

00:11:21.750 --> 00:11:25.330
Are you even aware of
the inconvenience you're causing?

00:11:25.330 --> 00:11:27.750
This grudge of yours is completely unwarranted.

00:11:27.750 --> 00:11:28.540
Excuse me?

00:11:28.540 --> 00:11:31.630
Viewing Roselia as your enemy is a mistake.

00:11:31.630 --> 00:11:34.380
Try to focus on improving your own band, instead.

00:11:34.380 --> 00:11:37.880
We don't have the time nor energy
to concern ourselves with you.

00:11:37.880 --> 00:11:40.040
And what exactly do YOU know?

00:11:40.040 --> 00:11:43.000
"We don't need a producer."
That's what Yukina said to me.

00:11:43.130 --> 00:11:47.880
To be honest... I don't think she meant to
single you out when she said that.

00:11:47.880 --> 00:11:49.210
Minato-san can be-

00:11:49.420 --> 00:11:50.920
But she rejected me, didn't she?!

00:11:50.920 --> 00:11:52.500
I'm going to make her recognize my talent!

00:11:52.500 --> 00:11:55.880
I'm going to defeat Roselia and prove I was right!

00:11:56.710 --> 00:11:58.330
Don't you have somewhere else to be?

00:11:58.330 --> 00:12:01.130
At this very moment, my members are hard at work.

00:12:01.130 --> 00:12:06.420
If you've got the time to argue with me,
then perhaps you should consider practicing more.

00:12:08.420 --> 00:12:10.170
Hina, we're leaving.

00:12:10.170 --> 00:12:11.580
Huh? Already?

00:12:11.580 --> 00:12:13.000
Don'tcha want some fries?

00:12:16.580 --> 00:12:19.330
Hi, LAYER-chan! See you later!

00:12:23.670 --> 00:12:27.170
I appreciate you taking the time to practice with me.

00:12:27.170 --> 00:12:31.130
You can practice solo whenever you want.
Havin' a partner is better.

00:12:32.710 --> 00:12:36.380
Invited Rei earlier, but it looks like she's not coming.

00:12:36.380 --> 00:12:37.830
Oh really...?

00:12:38.080 --> 00:12:41.130
Said she'd rather have some time alone to concentrate.

00:12:41.960 --> 00:12:44.790
What do you think about the showdown with Roselia?

00:12:45.250 --> 00:12:48.130
I don't mind competing against them
in the tournament,

00:12:48.130 --> 00:12:49.920
but I feel like this is getting out of control...

00:12:49.920 --> 00:12:52.580
That's just the hype talkin', don'tcha think?

00:12:52.580 --> 00:12:54.380
Do you agree with all this?

00:12:54.380 --> 00:12:55.880
I'm curious.

00:12:55.880 --> 00:12:59.080
I wanna know how far we can push ourselves
against a band like them.

00:12:59.380 --> 00:13:00.790
What about you?

00:13:04.460 --> 00:13:07.460
How do YOU feel about our upcoming show?

00:13:07.460 --> 00:13:08.580
Huh...?

00:13:09.750 --> 00:13:11.630
Honestly, I'm nervous.

00:13:12.080 --> 00:13:15.710
I've seen Roselia's talent shine on stage.

00:13:15.710 --> 00:13:17.920
The idea of sharing that stage is sort of intimidating...

00:13:19.330 --> 00:13:23.210
Plus, I might've found the people
I've been searching for...

00:13:24.080 --> 00:13:27.130
I think it'd be nice if we became the type of band
whose members are inseparable...

00:13:27.500 --> 00:13:33.880
And I want to work hard so that you and LAYER-san and
CHU2-san and PAREO-san all feel the same way.

00:13:36.330 --> 00:13:38.420
You ready to jam some more?

00:13:38.420 --> 00:13:40.500
Yes! Let's do it!

00:13:43.250 --> 00:13:44.750
Just the four of you?

00:13:44.750 --> 00:13:46.290
Well, uh...

00:13:47.330 --> 00:13:50.540
Sorry I'm late! My meeting ended up running over...

00:13:50.540 --> 00:13:51.540
Sayo-san!

00:13:51.540 --> 00:13:53.420
No need to apologize! You're five minutes early.

00:13:53.420 --> 00:13:54.500
Glad you could make it.

00:13:55.960 --> 00:13:58.710
Thank goodness!
We were worried you wouldn't come.

00:13:58.710 --> 00:14:00.580
I'm not one for skipping practice.

00:14:00.580 --> 00:14:04.250
Besides, we can't afford to lose to the likes of them.

00:14:11.750 --> 00:14:13.630
TWO tickets?

00:14:13.630 --> 00:14:18.000
Ako Udagawa-san and LOCK-san
each reserved one in your name.

00:14:18.000 --> 00:14:20.500
Sorry about that. I only need one...

00:14:20.500 --> 00:14:22.540
Atchan!

00:14:23.130 --> 00:14:24.460
Big Sis?!

00:14:24.460 --> 00:14:26.170
You here to see Ako and Rock?

00:14:26.170 --> 00:14:27.170
Yeah.

00:14:27.170 --> 00:14:28.790
The place is packed...

00:14:28.790 --> 00:14:31.750
Check it out!
Looks like that's where we put our stickers.

00:14:32.040 --> 00:14:33.710
Are we supposed to pick which band we like more?

00:14:33.710 --> 00:14:35.130
The band you're more excited to see.

00:14:36.790 --> 00:14:38.000
Where are you putting yours?

00:14:39.420 --> 00:14:40.420
In the middle...?

00:14:40.420 --> 00:14:41.540
I don't think that's an option...

00:14:41.540 --> 00:14:42.670
You have to choose.

00:14:42.670 --> 00:14:44.000
Yoo-hoo!

00:14:44.250 --> 00:14:46.880
This is how they're going to decide
who goes first, right?

00:14:46.880 --> 00:14:47.500
Yup.

00:14:47.500 --> 00:14:49.500
It's a big responsibility, you know!

00:14:49.750 --> 00:14:53.710
Dressing Room

00:14:51.880 --> 00:14:53.380
It's RAISE A SUILEN.

00:14:55.080 --> 00:14:56.540
We look forward to-

00:14:57.290 --> 00:14:58.630
Roselia?!

00:14:59.170 --> 00:15:01.210
What's going on? Did something happen?!

00:15:01.210 --> 00:15:03.130
You alright, kid?

00:15:04.040 --> 00:15:08.080
A throbbing stigma carving its way
through my right hand...

00:15:09.040 --> 00:15:11.170
I can't... remember the rest...

00:15:11.500 --> 00:15:14.000
You're awfully cute, ain'tcha?

00:15:14.210 --> 00:15:15.580
Masuki-san!

00:15:17.920 --> 00:15:20.670
Oh man, I can't believe we passed out again...

00:15:20.670 --> 00:15:22.710
You've caught us in quite the embarrassing state.

00:15:22.710 --> 00:15:25.080
And after you took the time to come say hello...

00:15:25.080 --> 00:15:26.210
Our apologies.

00:15:26.210 --> 00:15:30.250
We've got two different setlists
for whether we perform first or last,

00:15:30.250 --> 00:15:32.420
and I keep getting them confused...

00:15:32.420 --> 00:15:35.380
We just finished running through
the songs a little while ago.

00:15:35.380 --> 00:15:37.250
Two setlists...?!

00:15:37.250 --> 00:15:38.380
Udagawa-san!

00:15:38.380 --> 00:15:40.330
Wow, pretty impressive.

00:15:42.710 --> 00:15:45.960
Imai-san, would you like to provide
our guests with a snack?

00:15:45.960 --> 00:15:47.460
Oh, that's right!

00:15:48.040 --> 00:15:50.960
Ta-da! Me and Sayo made them.

00:15:50.960 --> 00:15:52.460
Cookies!

00:15:52.460 --> 00:15:53.880
These are homemade?!

00:15:53.880 --> 00:15:55.380
The icing looks professional.

00:15:55.380 --> 00:15:56.710
How cute!

00:15:57.460 --> 00:15:58.710
How the hell'd you get in here?!

00:15:58.710 --> 00:16:00.420
Through the door, of course!

00:16:00.420 --> 00:16:02.080
Would you like to eat with us?

00:16:02.080 --> 00:16:03.920
Thank you very much!

00:16:04.130 --> 00:16:05.250
A cat?

00:16:05.250 --> 00:16:07.750
A dog. We made cats, too.

00:16:07.750 --> 00:16:09.420
Help yourself, LAYER-san.

00:16:09.420 --> 00:16:10.670
Huh? Oh-

00:16:10.670 --> 00:16:11.580
No!

00:16:12.330 --> 00:16:14.420
Feeding the wildlife is strictly prohibited.

00:16:14.880 --> 00:16:17.130
The final results are in.

00:16:19.080 --> 00:16:19.670
Yukina!

00:16:19.670 --> 00:16:21.670
RAS! RAS! RAS!
Yukina!

00:16:21.670 --> 00:16:23.920
RAS! RAS! RAS!

00:16:24.330 --> 00:16:27.580
Roselia! Roselia!

00:16:32.500 --> 00:16:34.210
Big Sis!

00:16:34.210 --> 00:16:35.580
It's Roselia!

00:16:35.830 --> 00:16:37.750
Roselia's going first...?

00:16:39.500 --> 00:16:41.710
Good evening. We are Roselia.

00:16:43.210 --> 00:16:47.330
We're going to make sure
tonight's performance counts.

00:16:47.920 --> 00:16:49.250
Let's get started...

00:16:49.380 --> 00:16:50.290
"LOUDER."

00:16:51.040 --> 00:16:52.500
Dressing Room

00:16:54.330 --> 00:16:56.540
All according to my plan.

00:16:56.540 --> 00:16:58.830
We're the invincible final act!

00:16:58.830 --> 00:17:00.170
Where's LAYER-san?

00:17:01.500 --> 00:17:02.630
...itanda yo
...if it wasn't for you

00:17:02.630 --> 00:17:06.170
No more need to cry kitto
No more need to cry, that's right

00:17:06.170 --> 00:17:09.670
Feel alive...
Feel alive...

00:17:14.580 --> 00:17:19.130
RAS! RAS! RAS!

00:17:19.130 --> 00:17:21.040
On guitar: LOCK!

00:17:25.540 --> 00:17:26.630
Hey...

00:17:27.290 --> 00:17:28.500
You good?

00:17:28.500 --> 00:17:29.830
Y-yeah...

00:17:29.830 --> 00:17:34.710
The time has come for us to prove once and for all
that RAISE A SUILEN is better than Roselia.

00:17:35.080 --> 00:17:37.000
Beating Roselia to a pulp...

00:17:37.000 --> 00:17:39.080
RAS has the power to do that.

00:17:39.080 --> 00:17:40.920
We have the ultimate power!

00:17:41.210 --> 00:17:44.080
LOCK, your first performance is crucial.

00:17:44.080 --> 00:17:45.830
Tear the competition apart!

00:17:46.380 --> 00:17:47.380
Right!

00:17:47.380 --> 00:17:48.580
Let's get going.

00:17:48.960 --> 00:17:51.460
Um, should we huddle up first?

00:17:51.460 --> 00:17:52.540
Excuse me...?

00:17:52.830 --> 00:17:55.040
You know, a chant! A battle cry!

00:17:55.040 --> 00:17:58.000
Something like, "PasuPare, go!"

00:17:58.000 --> 00:17:59.000
Huh?

00:17:59.000 --> 00:18:00.750
No, not happening.

00:18:01.170 --> 00:18:03.290
I guess you're right...

00:18:04.250 --> 00:18:05.210
Let's do it.

00:18:05.420 --> 00:18:06.750
Oh, okay!

00:18:06.750 --> 00:18:09.170
I've always wanted to do a chant!

00:18:09.170 --> 00:18:10.330
C'mon, Rei.

00:18:10.330 --> 00:18:11.790
Huh? Oh...

00:18:14.080 --> 00:18:15.130
What do we do?

00:18:15.130 --> 00:18:16.250
Good question...

00:18:16.250 --> 00:18:18.080
U-um...

00:18:18.080 --> 00:18:20.210
Shall we just shout "RAISE A SUILEN"?

00:18:20.210 --> 00:18:23.960
R-RAISE A SUILEN!

00:18:25.000 --> 00:18:26.290
Talk about lame.

00:20:20.880 --> 00:20:22.000
Hey!
LOCK!

00:20:26.920 --> 00:20:28.710
That scared the crap outta me!

00:20:28.710 --> 00:20:30.830
Nerves must've done her in.

00:20:30.830 --> 00:20:32.790
Good thing she wasn't hurt.

00:20:32.790 --> 00:20:38.040
Anyhow... That was a sweet, excellent,
unstoppable performance!

00:20:38.330 --> 00:20:39.210
LAYER.

00:20:40.040 --> 00:20:42.790
That was your strongest show to date.

00:20:44.540 --> 00:20:45.710
Thanks...

00:20:47.290 --> 00:20:49.830
And now, the voting is about to begin...

00:20:51.670 --> 00:20:53.630
Both bands were incredible!

00:20:55.330 --> 00:20:57.460
You think Rock-chan's alright?

00:20:57.460 --> 00:20:59.830
She pushed herself too hard
with all that extra practice...

00:20:59.830 --> 00:21:02.330
They were awesome... Both of 'em.

00:21:02.330 --> 00:21:04.790
There was more passion in Rei's voice than usual...

00:21:05.880 --> 00:21:08.750
Thanks for sticking around, everyone.

00:21:08.750 --> 00:21:10.710
Have you cast your votes?

00:21:12.460 --> 00:21:14.830
How are you feeling at the moment, Yukina?

00:21:16.670 --> 00:21:19.380
Now then, let's announce the winner!

00:21:25.040 --> 00:21:26.290
Yes, yes, yes!

00:21:26.290 --> 00:21:26.960
Congratulations! Congratulations!
Yes, yes, yes!

00:21:26.960 --> 00:21:29.080
Congratulations! Congratulations!

00:21:29.290 --> 00:21:31.290
What do you think of THAT, Yukina?!

00:21:31.630 --> 00:21:36.330
With this, we've established our raison d'etre
and proven our music worthy of the crown!

00:21:38.080 --> 00:21:40.420
Even if I can't play it myself...

00:21:40.420 --> 00:21:41.210
Huh?

00:21:41.210 --> 00:21:42.790
I can't hear you!

00:21:43.420 --> 00:21:44.830
RAS! RAS!

00:21:44.830 --> 00:21:46.540
RAS! RAS! RAS!
RAS! RAS!

00:21:46.540 --> 00:21:46.880
RAS! RAS! RAS!

00:21:46.880 --> 00:21:48.080
RAS! RAS! RAS!
Rin-Rin...

00:21:48.080 --> 00:21:49.000
RAS! RAS! RAS!

00:21:56.170 --> 00:22:08.080
Yume uchinuku shunkan ni kimi wa nani o omou no?

00:22:10.210 --> 00:22:12.380
La la la la la la...

00:22:12.540 --> 00:22:14.750
La la la la la la...

00:22:14.960 --> 00:22:17.080
La la la la la la...

00:22:17.080 --> 00:22:19.170
La la la...

00:22:19.170 --> 00:22:23.880
Hashaginagara itsudemo oikaketeta

00:22:23.880 --> 00:22:28.330
Honoka ni hikaru yume no kakera

00:22:28.630 --> 00:22:33.290
Zenbu hiroiatsumete tsunaidemita

00:22:33.290 --> 00:22:38.580
Minna o terasu hoshi ni natta

00:22:38.580 --> 00:22:43.540
Kirameku omoidetachi dakishime

00:22:43.540 --> 00:22:48.420
Fumidasu kimi no senaka itooshii

00:22:48.420 --> 00:22:49.080
Dakara?

00:22:49.080 --> 00:22:53.790
Dare yori mo (kimi to) itsumademo (issho ni)

00:22:53.790 --> 00:22:58.540
Ima kara (minna de) utau yo (sei no de)

00:22:58.540 --> 00:23:02.210
Kore ijou matenai kara?

00:23:02.210 --> 00:23:03.130
"Sei no!"

00:23:03.130 --> 00:23:08.040
Aoi sora ni Yes! BanG! Dream! (Sono yume)

00:23:08.040 --> 00:23:12.880
Kaze ni yureru yuuki no uta (Uchinuke!)

00:23:12.880 --> 00:23:22.130
Yakusoku shita ano basho to kimi o tsunaida melody

00:23:34.330 --> 00:23:37.630
Next Time: Save Them in the Music
